1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
One missed defect.

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:04,000
One Million Lives.

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,000
How do you find what you can't see?

4
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Welcome to ScanMaster Training.

5
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:13,000
In the next three minutes, you'll understand the entire field of ultrasonic testing

6
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,000
without touching the software yet.

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,000
This is Video one.

8
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:18,000
No prerequisites.

9
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Let's start.

10
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Ultrasonic Testing, U-T for short,

11
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:27,000
is how engineers see inside solid metal.

12
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Think of it like sonar for a submarine.

13
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:35,000
But instead of the ocean, we're scanning a jet engine, a pipeline, or a steel plate.

14
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:37,000
Sound waves go in.

15
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Echoes come back.

16
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:43,000
The Echoes tell us if there's a crack, avoid, or just clean material.

17
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:47,000
Every U-T inspection has exactly four players.

18
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Let's meet them.

19
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:49,000
One.

20
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:50,000
The Pulsar.

21
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:54,000
A small electronic box that fires high voltage pulses.

22
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:57,000
In ScanMaster, this is the RPP3.

23
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:58,000
Two.

24
00:00:58,000 --> 00:00:59,000
The Transducer.

25
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:04,000
The probe that converts those electric pulses into actual sound waves

26
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:07,000
and listens for the Echoes coming back.

27
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Three.

28
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:10,000
The Part Under Test.

29
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:13,000
Could be a plate, a tube, a forging.

30
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Anything you need to verify.

31
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:16,000
And four.

32
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:18,000
The Receiver and Display.

33
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:21,000
In ScanMaster, the UPR100 board

34
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:25,000
and the MCIO software you're learning to use.

35
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:29,000
These four players working together give you the A-scan.

36
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:32,000
The most important graph you'll ever read.

37
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:35,000
U-T matters because it's non-destructive.

38
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:36,000
The part stays whole.

39
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:38,000
It goes back into service.

40
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:43,000
And you've proven it's safe to fly, to pressurize, to carry load.

41
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Every aerospace primary structure, every nuclear pressure vessel, every offshore weld,

42
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:52,000
checked this way.

43
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:56,000
Every inspection you'll ever run follows the same five steps.

44
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:58,000
Memorize this list.

45
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:01,000
It's the spine of every video that follows.

46
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:02,000
Step one.

47
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:05,000
Set up the time base and the material.

48
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:08,000
Tell the system what you're scanning and how deep to look.

49
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:10,000
Step two.

50
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:12,000
Configure the pulsar and the receiver.

51
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:16,000
Pick the right frequency, the right voltage, the right filter.

52
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:17,000
Step three.

53
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:19,000
Tune the gain.

54
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:22,000
And if your part is thick, add TCG.

55
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:24,000
Time corrected gain.

56
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:26,000
Step four.

57
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:28,000
Place gates over the signals that matter.

58
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:32,000
Gates are how you decide what's a pass and what's a fail.

59
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:34,000
Step five.

60
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:35,000
Save the setup.

61
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:36,000
Run the scan.

62
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:38,000
Review the result.

63
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:40,000
One mistake beginners make.

64
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:42,000
They jump straight to the gates.

65
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:46,000
But if your time base is wrong, your material velocity is wrong.

66
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:48,000
Or your gain is wrong.

67
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:51,000
Then every gate you place is measuring nonsense.

68
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:53,000
The order matters.

69
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:54,000
Quick recap.

70
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:57,000
UT is sonar for solids.

71
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:58,000
Four players.

72
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:01,000
Pulsar, transducer, part, and receiver.

73
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:03,000
Five steps.

74
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:04,000
Always in order.

75
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:05,000
Next up.

76
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:07,000
Meet the ScanMaster system.

77
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:12,000
We'll open the software and tour every tab you'll be using.

